## Appendix A — Files

**New shared files**, each mirroring a perpetuals file:

| New file | Mirrors | Holds |
|---|---|---|
| `core/data_type/option_info.py` | `funding_info.py` | `OptionInfo` (mark, IV, Greeks, open interest), `OptionInstrumentInfo` (strike, expiry, call/put) |
| `core/data_type/option_api_order_book_data_source.py` | `perpetual_api_order_book_data_source.py` | Adds the option-info stream to the order-book source |
| `connector/options_trading.py` | `perpetual_trading.py` | Positions, live option info, chain index |
| `connector/option_derivative_py_base.py` | `perpetual_derivative_py_base.py` | Base connector: info listener, expiry and settlement, `get_option_chain`, `get_option_info`, `get_underlying_price` |
| `connector/derivative/option_budget_checker.py` | `perpetual_budget_checker.py` | Premium for buys, margin estimate for sells |

**Changed files**

- `core/event/events.py`: add `OptionExpired` and `OptionSettled`. Plain Python, no Cython rebuild. Avoid enum numbers 213–215 (used on the wallet-transfer branch).
- `connector/markets_recorder.py`: record `OptionSettled`, so settlements reach trade history.
- Scripts only receive a fixed list of events, so the options layer adds a helper to subscribe to the new ones. It must keep a reference to its listener: listeners are held weakly and otherwise disappear.
- No change to the Cython trading-rule layer: option details live in `OptionInstrumentInfo`, and the collateral fields already exist.

**`delta_options` connector**, same 8-file layout as `delta_perpetual`:

- Reused: signing, networking (including proxy), response unwrapping, order placement and cancellation, time sync, WebSocket plumbing.
- New: calls/puts product filter, name mapping, Greeks/IV feed, chain helper (called from a script's `init_markets`, before the connector starts), expiry and settlement detection, fee and margin estimates.

## Appendix B — Live check (June 2026, read-only)

Against `https://api.india.delta.exchange`:

- 924 live options (BTC 634, ETH 290), calls and puts.
- Daily, weekly and monthly expiries, all at 12:00 UTC.
- European-style, cash-settled in USD, same collateral as our perps.
- The `C-BTC-63800-130626` ticker included mark price; bid, ask and mark IV; delta, gamma, theta, vega, rho; spot index; open interest; price bands.
- Same response format, signing and integer contract sizing (`contract_value`) as `delta_perpetual`.

